                        "form": "xiphias"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a220d128-e3e4-300c-b615-3aeaeb0093dd",
                        "entry_id": "b3c764e7-e0b1-35c7-bb8a-e69f2e6c1452",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of swordfish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d1e9269-c6de-48a0-bcea-d4ef12eda459",
                                "sense_id": "a220d128-e3e4-300c-b615-3aeaeb0093dd",
                                "text": "Huge Ziffius, whom Mariners eschew / No lesse, then rockes, as travellers informe […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b7eb5a9-66f7-4709-9415-42c83f36147c",
                                "sense_id": "a220d128-e3e4-300c-b615-3aeaeb0093dd",
                                "text": "S. Malpighi having dissected the Head of a Xiphias or Sword Fish, which hath a very big Eye, observ'd that the middle of the Optick Nerve is nothing else, but a large Membrane, folded according to its length in many Doubles almost like a Fan, and invested by the Dura Mater."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8549790-2f1d-4ff0-8c3a-9cf4eeb8f500",
                                "sense_id": "a220d128-e3e4-300c-b615-3aeaeb0093dd",
                                "text": "Trebius Niger informs us that […] the xiphias, or, in other words, the sword-fish, has a sharp-pointed muzzle, with which it is able to pierce the sides of a ship and send it to the bottom […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "222b6c97-3288-43a6-b31a-ce8c86428f66",
                                "sense_id": "a220d128-e3e4-300c-b615-3aeaeb0093dd",
                                "text": "In the xiphias, you observe, the enormous elongation of the head is produced by the elongation of the jaws proper – that is to say, of the pre-maxilla and nasal bones."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
